## Summary & Motivation

Adds support for [refinements](https://cloud.google.com/looker/docs/lookml-refinements) (which let you modify an explore or view after creating it) and [extends](https://cloud.google.com/looker/docs/reusing-code-with-extends) (which let you extend views or explores to create new ones):

```lkml
view: base {
  sql_table_name: `prod.base_data` ;;
  description: "This is the base view"

  dimension: email {
    type: string
    sql: ${TABLE}.email ;;
  }

  dimension: name {
    hidden: yes
    type: string
    sql: ${TABLE}.name ;;
  }
}

# Modify base to change table name, show name dimension
view: +base {
  sql_table_name: `prod.new_base_data` ;;

  dimension: name {
    hidden: no
    type: string
    sql: ${TABLE}.name ;;
  }
}
```

We now merge any changes from refinements into the config of the explore or view before converting it to a spec. For explores or views which extend other models, we topo sort all explores/views based on extend dependencies and merge them accordingly.

